{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "MRK",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then came together to him the Pharisees, and certain of the scribes, who came from Jerusalem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when they saw some of his disciples eating bread with defiled (that is to say with unwashed) hands, they found fault.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the Pharisees, and all the Jews, except they wash ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hands often eat not, holding the tradition of the elders.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "when they come",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from the market, except they wash, they eat not. And many other things there are, which they have received to hold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the washing of cups, and pots, and of brazen vessels, and tables.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then the Pharisees and scribes asked him, Why walk not thy disciples according to the tradition of the elders, but eat bread with unwashed hands?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He answered and said to them, Well hath Isaiah prophesied concerning you hypocrites, as it is written, This people honoreth me with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " lips, but their heart is far from me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But, in vain do they worship me, teaching ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " doctrines the commandments of men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For laying aside the commandment of God, ye hold the tradition of men, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the washing of pots and cups: and many other such like things ye do.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to them, Full well ye reject the commandment of God, that ye may keep your own tradition,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Moses said, Honor thy father and thy mother; and, Whoever curseth father or mother, let him die the death:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But ye say, If a man shall say to his father or mother, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Corban, that is to say, a gift, by whatever thou mightest be profited by me; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he shall be free",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ye suffer him no more to do aught for his father or his mother;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Making the word of God of no effect through your traditions, which ye have delivered: and many such like things ye do.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he had called all the people ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", he said to them, Hearken to me every one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of you",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and understand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There is nothing from without a man, that entering into him, can defile him: but the things which come out of him, those are they that defile the man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If any man hath ears to hear, let him hear.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when he had entered into the house from the people, his disciples asked him concerning the parable.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he saith to them, Are ye so void of understanding also? Do ye not perceive, that whatever thing from without entereth into the man, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cannot defile him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because it entereth not into his heart, but into the belly, and goeth out into the draught, purging all kinds of food.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, That which cometh out of the man, that defileth the man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For from within, out of the heart of men, proceed evil thoughts, adulteries, fornications, murders,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thefts, covetousness, wickedness, deceit, lasciviousness, an evil eye, blasphemy, pride, foolishness;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All these evil things come from within, and defile the man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And from thence he arose, and went into the borders of Tyre and Sidon, and entered into a house, and would have no man know ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": but he could not be hid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For a certain woman, whose young daughter had an unclean spirit, heard of him, and came and fell at his feet:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(The woman was a Greek, a Syrophenician by nation,) and she besought him that he would cast forth the demon out of her daughter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Jesus said to her, Let the children first be satisfied: for it is not meet to take the children's bread, and to cast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the dogs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And she answered and said to him, Yes, Lord: yet the dogs under the table eat of the children's crums.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to her, For this saying, depart; the demon is gone out of thy daughter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when she had come to her house, she found the demon had gone out, and her daughter laid upon the bed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And again, departing from the borders of Tyre and Sidon, he came to the sea of Galilee, through the midst of the borders of Decapolis.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they bring to him one that was deaf, and had an impediment in his speech; and they beseech him to put his hand upon him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he took him aside from the multitude, and put his fingers into his ears, and he spit, and touched his tongue.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And looking up to heaven, he sighed, and saith to him, Effatha, that is, Be opened.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And immediately his ears were opened, and the string of his tongue was loosed, and he spoke plain.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he charged them that they should tell no man: but the more he charged them; so much the more a great deal they published ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ";",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MRK.7.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:MRK.7.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And were beyond measure astonished, saying, He hath done all things well; he maketh both the deaf to hear, and the dumb to speak.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
